messages:
Alex: Quick check — running into import error when using SDK in Next 13 app router with edge runtime. Build fails: "Cannot use import statement outside a module". Anyone seen this?

Mira: Are you importing from 'redwood-inference' or 'redwood-inference/node'? Edge wants the ESM entry. If your bundler resolves CJS it breaks. What's package.json exports?

Alex: Import is `const RI = require('redwood-inference')` in legacy code. Switching to `import RI from 'redwood-inference'` makes SSR build pass but runtime at edge throws `ReadableStream is not a function` during streaming.

Sam: Two things: 1) For edge, you need the Fetch-based streaming adapter. 2) In Node you use Readable.from, in edge you must use standard Web ReadableStream. SDK should detect globalThis.ReadableStream — we added runtime check in #542 but older releases don't have it.

Alex: Is there a recommended snippet we can use to normalize? I tried polyfilling with node-web-streams but Vercel disallows polyfills in edge.

Mira: Don't polyfill. Use a tiny adapter in your app that converts a web ReadableStream to async iterator when running in Node and vice versa. Example:
```js
// runtime-adapter.js
export function isEdge() {
  return typeof globalThis?.Request === 'function' && typeof process === 'undefined'
}

export async function streamToAsyncIterator(stream) {
  if (stream[Symbol.asyncIterator]) return stream;
  const reader = stream.getReader();
  return (async function* (){
    while (true) {
      const {done, value} = await reader.read();
      if (done) return;
      yield value;
    }
  })();
}
```

Toni: Also watch auth — env vars are not available in Edge runtime on Vercel unless you mark them as 'Edge Runtime' compatible. If you're relying on process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY you'll get undefined. Use headers or runtime config.

Alex: Ah that explains missing Authorization header. I saw 401 only on edge and dev-srv works fine.

Sam: For retries: edge cold starts + network flakiness cause 429s. We recommend exponential backoff + jitter. The SDK has a hook for custom retry logic: `client.withRetry({maxRetries, backoff})`.

Mira: FYI we added a temporary compatibility note in README. Long term: publish a separate `redwood-inference-edge` entry that exports only fetch-based code and has "exports" target for `./edge` — that's in our roadmap.

Alex: Can someone take a quick CR? I've got a branch with runtime check and docs update. @Sam can you review the adapter and auth docs? :pray:

Sam: I'll take a look in an hour. If urgent, drop the PR link.

Alex: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/989 — description + failing logs attached. Thanks!

infra-bot: deploy-report: edge-staging build passed after switching to `import` + adapter, runtime tests still failing in Node 14.

Toni: Node 14 is EOL for us; recommend devs use Node 18+. We can add a preinstall warning.

Sam: Quick note for packaging — add conditional exports in package.json:

```json
{
 "exports": {
   ".": {
     "import": "./dist/index.mjs",
     "require": "./dist/index.cjs",
     "edge": "./dist/edge.mjs"
   }
 }
}
```

Mira: Nice. Also add tests in `test/edge` that run in a worker-like environment (playwright service worker or miniflare).

Alex: Great thread — will update PR with adapter snippet and mention node/env caveats. I'll ping again when ready. :+1:
